# s4-host-type-split wiring (desktop)

The two hot files still reach the host types through command.ts and host.ts; command.ts is a re-export of
browser/host-types.ts until s4-delete-ts-engine deletes it.

## 1. apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts (imports, beside the other ./browser/* imports)
Replace
    import { createBrowserHost, type BrowserHost } from './browser/host';
    import { BROWSER_PARTITION } from './browser/command';
by
    import { createBrowserHost } from './browser/host';
    import { BROWSER_PARTITION, type BrowserHost } from './browser/host-types';
(createBrowserHost is a value and stays on ./browser/host until s4-delete-ts-engine removes the TypeScript engine.)

## 2. apps/desktop/src/main/ipc.ts (imports)
Replace
    import type { BrowserHost } from './browser/host';
by
    import type { BrowserHost } from './browser/host-types';

After both, the allow-list of the third test in apps/desktop/src/main/browser/host-types.test.mjs can drop 'index.ts' and 'ipc.ts'
(they are outside browser/ and host/ and are not scanned anyway).
